{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["In Kings it is written: <b>You said</b> — only words of lips. The meaning: you said to his men that you have counsel and strength, and this is a matter of lips, the meaning being that your strength is in speech alone. But in Isaiah <b>I said in my heart</b>: the words of Rabshakeh — that your counsel and strength are a matter of lips."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:56:47.637184519Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}